    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0577" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg567"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 905.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 7, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In your despatch No. 628 you have given me
                    an account of the proceedings of the Scottish tribunal at Edinburgh, against the
                    Pampero. The just opinions so clearly expressed by the court in that case serve
                    to augment the regret which this government feels that the cause of
                    international peace and harmony have suffered so deeply from the want of equal
                    clearness and decision in the proceedings of the courts of London in the case of
                    the Alexandra. I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">C. F. Adams</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
